157 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (The Knapsack Optimisation System is an educational Python mini project that solves the 0/1 Knapsack Problem. Given items with individual non-negative integer weights and values and a knapsack with limited capacity, the program determines the subset with maximum total value without exceeding the capacity. Each item may be selected at most once.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
158 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (The proposed solution uses Dynamic Programming to build a two-dimensional table of optimal values for progressively larger item subsets and capacities. Backtracking through this table identifies the selected items. The conventional implementation takes O\(nW\) time and O\(nW\) space for n items and integer capacity W.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
159 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (The system demonstrates input validation, recurrence formulation, exact optimization, solution reconstruction and algorithm analysis. It is intended for classroom demonstrations and modest integer capacities. Python 3 is used for the implementation.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
