521 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 107 0 R
/E (The Knapsack Optimisation System demonstrates how Dynamic Programming solves a constrained selection problem by decomposing it into smaller overlapping subproblems. The Python implementation accepts items and a capacity, constructs a table of optimal values, and reconstructs a valid selection with the maximum achievable total value.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
522 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 107 0 R
/E (The project reinforces fundamental DAA concepts including problem formulation, state transitions, recurrence relations, correctness-oriented testing and time-space complexity. The worked example illustrates how selecting items 2 and 3 gives value 220 within capacity 50.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
523 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 107 0 R
/E (The full DP table is practical for moderate integer capacities but can consume substantial resources for large inputs. Future extensions could use memory optimization, additional optimization techniques and an improved graphical user interface. Overall, the project provides a useful academic foundation for understanding exact combinatorial optimization using Python.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
